"explanation": "The statement 'Let them eat cake' (or 'brioche') is a famous historical misattribution to Marie Antoinette. Historical evidence indicates that the phrase first appears in Jean-Jacques Rousseau's *Confessions*, written in 1765. In this text, Rousseau attributes the remark to an unnamed 'great princess of France' during a bread shortage. Since Marie Antoinette was only seven years old in 1765 and had not yet arrived in France (she arrived in 1770), she could not have been the speaker. Scholars generally believe Rousseau was referring to an earlier queen, most plausibly Maria Theresa of Spain (wife of Louis XV). Therefore, the statement was attributed by Rousseau to a princess, not actually said by Marie Antoinette.",
